    "---\n",
    "## Section 7: One-Click Pipeline Runner\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of running each section individually, you can call the `run_pipeline_v2()` convenience function which orchestrates **all** steps — from data loading through to report generation. This is the same entry point used by the CLI:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "python qf/timeseries/gap_filling_v2.py --target MSFT\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### What the Pipeline Does\n",
    "\n",
    "| Step | Description |\n",
    "|------|-------------|\n",
    "| **1** | Load data & select peers (`load_data` + `select_peers`) |\n",
    "| **2** | Build price panel & inject sinusoidal distress |\n",
    "| **3** | Run all non-linear reconstructions (static, dynamic, ML, ensemble, optimised) |\n",
    "| **4** | Evaluate & rank methods (RMSE, MAE, Return Corr, Vol Ratio) |\n",
    "| **5** | Apply drift corrections to the best method |\n",
    "| **6** | Backtest mean-reversion strategy across all reconstructions |\n",
